Cloud-Sharing Credential Campaign — IG-2026-004

Status: 🔴 Active / Campaign
Sector: Cross-sector
Region: Global
Incident Type: Credential compromise campaign
Threat Actor: Zestix / Sentap
Primary Platforms: ShareFile, ownCloud, Nextcloud
Last Reviewed: August 2026

A threat actor tracked as Zestix, also known as Sentap, has been linked to a campaign targeting corporate cloud file-sharing environments using previously stolen credentials rather than software exploits. Researchers reported that credentials were harvested from employee systems infected with information-stealing malware including RedLine, Lumma, and Vidar. The stolen credentials were then used to authenticate to exposed ShareFile, ownCloud, and Nextcloud instances.

Researchers associated the campaign with approximately 50 organizations spanning aviation, defense, healthcare, utilities, public transportation, telecommunications, legal services, real estate, government, and other sectors.

Confirmed / strongly corroborated attack characteristics:

Valid credentials obtained from infostealer logs
ShareFile, ownCloud, and Nextcloud environments targeted
Corporate files accessed
Stolen datasets offered for sale
MFA was reportedly absent from affected accounts
No platform zero-day was required in the documented ownCloud cases

Watching for:

Additional named victims
Final victim count
Vendor disclosures
Evidence of downstream intrusions
Credential age at time of compromise
Session/token abuse
Identity-provider logging
Law-enforcement action
Whether affected organizations rotate or invalidate exposed credentials

